/target
# Cargo.lock IS tracked: this crate ships binaries (simble, the MCP server)
# and examples, so a reproducible dependency graph matters more than letting
# downstream library users resolve their own. Without it CI resolved different
# versions than any developer did.

# Generated in CI for the Pages deploy, never committed.
/web/pkg/
/web/doc/
**/*.rs.bk
.DS_Store
*.swp
*~

# Staged by the Pages workflow from the top-level catalog/ (see pages.yml).
/web/catalog/

# tests/interop/bumble_link.py is imported by the scripts beside it, so
# running any of them leaves a bytecode cache here.
/tests/interop/__pycache__/

# Local Python virtualenv for the interop scripts (see tests/interop/README.md).
# A convenience for running them, never a dependency: CI just pip-installs bumble.
.venv/
